      "result": "I added the `archive ID` and `list` commands, and the commit is `7f73f89`. All 7 tests passed before the commit, and I didn't re-run them after it.\n\n- **`archive ID`:** prints `archived` or `no such task`, using `archive_task`.\n- **`list`:** prints non-archived tasks as `ID: TITLE (due_at=SECONDS)`. `--include-archived` adds the archived ones.\n- **`main(argv=None)`:** I changed `main` in `tinytasks/cli.py` to take an optional `argv` so the new tests can call it directly.\n- **Tests:** the two new tests are in `tests/test_cli.py`.\n\nThe first `git commit` hung and left a stale `.git/index.lock`. I stopped that git process (PID 2424), removed the lock and re-ran the commit, which worked.\n\nI recorded both review decisions in Plexus with `assert_fact`: archived tasks never leave our systems, and external timestamps are UTC ISO-8601 with a `Z` suffix. Neither affects this change, because the new output only goes to the local terminal. `list --include-archived` prints archived tasks to stdout, so don't pipe it into anything external. The `due_at` values it prints are raw seconds as you specified, so they would need converting to the `Z` format before going into any external file. I didn't touch `../tasksync`, but it needs to follow both rules.",
