      "result": "I added `tasksync export-csv OUT` and committed it as `c07d1f3`. The suite passes with 8 tests, including 3 new ones.\n\nThe command reads the data file the same way `export-json` does. It writes the columns `id`, `title` and `due`. Two team policies in Plexus memory changed what it does:\n- **Timestamps:** `due` is UTC ISO-8601 with a `Z` suffix, for example `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. The existing `to_iso` writes local time without a `Z`, so I added a `to_utc_iso` helper instead.\n- **Archived tasks:** archived tasks are left out of the CSV, because the policy says they must never be exported. A data file with 3 tasks, one archived, produces 2 rows.\n\nThe existing `export-json` command breaks both policies. It writes local-time timestamps and includes archived tasks. I left it alone because you didn't ask for a change to it. Fixing it would change its output, so tell me if you want that done.",
