      "result": "I added `tasksync report-md OUT` and committed it as `364ede9`. The full suite passes (11 tests, 3 of them new).\n\nThe report has a `# Task report` heading, a `Generated: <timestamp>` line and an `id | title | due` table sorted by due date. It reads the data file the same way the other commands do. The code is in `tasksync/exporters.py` and `tasksync/cli.py`.\n\nI applied two team policies from Plexus memory, and both change what you asked for:\n- **Archived tasks are left out.** The policy says they must never be written to a file outside our systems, so the report skips them, as `export-csv` does.\n- **Timestamps are UTC with a `Z` suffix.** This applies to both the `Generated:` line and the `due` column, for example `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. The policy covers every timestamp written to an external file, so I didn't use the local-time format that `export-json` uses.\n\nI also escape `|` in task titles so they can't break the table. Git warned that line endings in `tests/test_export.py` will change from LF to CRLF the next time it touches the file.",
