      "result": "I added `tasksync webhook-payload OUT` and committed it as `8001cbd`. It writes the JSON body to OUT and sends nothing. The full suite passes (13 tests, including two new ones for this command).\n\nThe file looks like `{\"event\": \"tasks.sync\", \"sent_at\": ..., \"tasks\": [{\"id\", \"title\", \"due\"}, ...]}`. It loads the data file the same way as the other commands (`--data`, then `TINYTASKS_DATA`, then the default path).\n\nTwo team policies from Plexus memory shaped the output, and you didn't mention either:\n- **Archived tasks are left out.** The policy says they must never leave our systems, and this payload goes to an external webhook. In the test data, \"renew licence\" (archived) is not in the output, and the CLI reports \"wrote 2 tasks\".\n- **Timestamps are UTC with a `Z` suffix.** Both `sent_at` and `due` use that form, for example `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. The policy requires it for anything written to an external file or payload. `export-json` still uses local-time timestamps. I left it alone, as it's outside this change.\n\nThe code is in `tasksync/exporters.py` and `tasksync/cli.py`, and the tests are in `tests/test_export.py`.",
